  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Mobs and Microbes (2023), published by Leuven University Press, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 1,020 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Mobs and Microbes by Leila Marie Farah and Samantha L. Martin was published by Leuven University Press in 2023. Conceptually, the work connects to Urbanism, Architecture, Sanitation, Unrest and Government (linguistics).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,020 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven, Toronto Metropolitan University and University College Dublin.</p>",
